:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-2)+2=0.$" 13194139535450 true] [17592186349688 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349689 13194139535450 true] [17592186349688 1089 "q-112197" 13194139535450 true] [17592186349688 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535450 true] [17592186349688 1100 "Find the vector $x$, if $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535450 true] [17592186349688 1113 #uuid "17dc6e1e-fced-5fcf-b2a9-5b0d39b0426e" 13194139535450 true] [17592186349688 1145 "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,6\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,-7\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -30 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 21 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535450 true] [